{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213421,"nonce":"krNXKnDoMpfAYsLDPpPk6Lw+Wf0=","title":"Module registry, call cells, epochs, reload pipeline and events","message":"The core owns the lang:path namespace (LangId is a registry: Zyntax registers\none per grammar snapshot), per-module function tables, and hot reload.\n\nEvery call that crosses a module or language boundary goes through a\nper-function atomic call cell; a tier may inline within a module. Compiled\ncode is repointed with beadie swap_compiled / reload; old code is freed by\nthe core's code allocator at the next quiescent point.\n\nEach TypeDesc carries an epoch; inline caches and synthesised classes key on\n(desc, epoch), so one increment invalidates every cache in every language.\n\nPipeline: trigger (reactor watch, signal, API) -\u003e adapter diff (ash: bytecode\nhash; wren: module re-run with class identity kept; zyntax: HIR fingerprint)\n-\u003e ReloadPlan -\u003e quiescent point -\u003e patch cells and epochs -\u003e before/after\nhooks -\u003e Reload event to all subscribers. Layout changes: per-adapter policy,\ndecline or re-run in v1. Added and removed functions applied (ash computes\nthem and drops them today).\n\nMaking the Cranelift tier reloadable through cells is what lets LLVM leave the\ndevelopment build without losing reload.","files":null}]}